<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">American Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1765">1765</a>–<a href="/years/1783">1783</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as American War of Independence, American Revolutionary War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The American Revolution was the rebellion of thirteen British colonies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, which declared independence in 1776 and won it in the war that ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1783">Treaty of Paris</a> in 1783. Most Iroquois nations sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and lost their lands, while tens of thousands of Loyalists moved north, leading to new colonies such as Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> and Cape Breton.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/american-revolution.jpg" alt="American Revolution" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Trumbull · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Declaration_of_Independence_(1819),_by_John_Trumbull.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
